<title>POLAND: POLISH CURRENCY RESERVES RISE TO $21.55 BLN IN FEB.</title>
<headline>POLISH CURRENCY RESERVES RISE TO $21.55 BLN IN FEB.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish net foreign currency</p>
<p>reserves grew by $73 million in February to $21.55 billion and</p>
<p>were $203 million lower than a year ago, the National Bank of</p>
<p>Poland said.</p>
<p>It said official reserves fell by $121 million in the</p>
<p>January-February period compared to a $1.31 billion rise in the</p>
<p>corresponding period of last year.</p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dlrs)  FEBRUARY   JANUARY  FEBRUARY 96</p>
<p>    Official reserves		  NA	  18.21     17.01</p>
<p>    Net reserves		     21.55	 21.47     21.75</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves</p>
<p>are those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount</p>
<p>of hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
